---
title: Poppy Seed Bagels
description: Chewy gluten-free bagels with a poppy-seed crunch, from Adult Lunches (p38). Nut free.
source: Adult Lunches cookbook, p38 (transcribed from a photo)
servings: 10
time required: 50 minutes
prep time: 20 minutes
cook time: 50 minutes
difficulty: intermediate
course: lunch
diet: gluten-free, nut-free, vegetarian
tags: bread, bagels, gluten-free, nut-free, lunch
locale: en_AU
---

Combine @gluten-free plain flour{450%g}(sifted), @potato flour{75%g}, @white rice flour{90%g}, @buckwheat flour{75%g}, @dried yeast{10%g}, @salt{2%tsp} and @xanthan gum{2%tsp} in a #large bowl{}.

Place @egg{1}, @egg whites{3}(reserve the yolks), @light olive oil{180%ml} and @warm milk{375%ml} in a #large bowl of an electric mixer{}; beat on medium speed for ~{3.5%minutes}. Add the flour mixture, 1 cup at a time, beating until combined and smooth.

Turn the dough onto a lightly floured surface and knead until smooth. Divide the dough into 10 pieces. Roll each piece into a 24 cm (9½-inch) long rope. Working with one length of dough at a time, shape into a ring until the ends meet, securing ends together with a little @water{}.

Place the rings on a #greased oven tray{}. Repeat with the remaining dough. Cover with oiled plastic wrap; stand in a warm place for ~{45%minutes}.

Preheat the #oven{} to 200°C/400°F. Grease two #oven trays{} then line with #baking paper{}.

Working in batches of four, drop the bagels one by one into a #large saucepan{} of @boiling water{}, ensuring they don't touch; boil for ~{1%minute}. Turn the bagels over; boil for another ~{1%minute}. Using a #slotted spoon{}, transfer the bagels to the lined trays. Repeat with the remaining bagels.

Brush the tops of the bagels with combined reserved @egg yolks{3} and the extra @warm milk{1%tbsp}; sprinkle with @poppy seeds{2%tsp} and @flaked sea salt{2%tsp}. Bake for ~{25%minutes} or until golden. Cool on a #wire rack{}.

> Serving suggestion: serve lightly toasted, topped with smashed avocado, roasted cherry tomatoes, crumbled feta and fresh oregano leaves, or simply spread with cream cheese or jam.

> Nutritional count per bagel: 1914 kJ (458 cal); 54.9 g carbohydrate; 8.8 g protein; 0.7 g fibre; 21.8 g total fat (4.5 g saturated fat).
